Modified by Republic contributors for a Python 3.11+ single-call SDK:
removed agent, hook, replay, UI, telemetry, tool execution and client persistence;
replaced generic request/executor machinery with one Provider protocol; retained
text/file/reasoning/tool data and block-based event aggregation; added strict
event ordering, detached snapshots, recursive metadata merging, unknown usage,
explicit response identity and deterministic stream cleanup. Files use tagged
URL/base64 strings. Tool arguments remain raw strings, including invalid JSON.
Tests retain relevant aggregation, metadata, missing-terminal and early-exit
scenarios and add interleaving and cancellation coverage. This is a modified
subset, not a claim of upstream API or behavior compatibility.
